is hypothesis across the examples.\n\n**Revising Output Priority**\n\nMy previous priority order hypothesis (7>8>4>6) appears incorrect. Examining Ex 4 and Ex 5, specifically outputs for cells where TL is 0, it seems 4 actually overrides 8, not the other way around. This significantly changes the established hierarchy.\n\n**Establishing Output Priority**\n\nMy previous priority hypothesis was incorrect. I've now definitively established the output color priority as 7 > 4 > 8 > 6 > 0, based on the observed interactions between quadrant colors and their impact on the final output matrix values across all provided examples.\n\n**Applying Output Priority**\n\nI have successfully applied the established priority order (7 > 4 > 8 > 6 > 0) to a test case. The calculated output matrix aligns with the expected values, confirming the derived priority scheme. My current focus is to re-verify this with the remaining examples.\n\n",
